# Live output

`DumpContainer` and `Util.ProgressBar` update one block in the **Results** tab in place
instead of appending a new block on every change. The script runs for about one second
and only writes to the output panel.

```csharp run
var progress = new Util.ProgressBar(0, "Processing items").Dump();
var status = new DumpContainer("Starting...");
status.Dump("Status");

var processed = new List<int>();
for (var step = 1; step <= 5; step++)
{
    Thread.Sleep(200);
    processed.Add(step * 10);
    progress.PercentComplete = step * 20;
    status.Content = $"Processed {processed.Count} of 5 items";
}

progress.Caption = "Done";
processed.Dump("Processed values", 1);
```
